  "keyTakeaways": [
    "Soda ash (2836.20) is the largest U.S. Chapter 28 export at $1.47B but fell 14.1% in 2025; Mexico, Chile and Brazil are the biggest buyers of U.S. carbonates (2836), and since April 24, 2026 Mexico charges 35% on soda ash from countries without a trade agreement while qualifying U.S. soda ash stays free under USMCA.",
    "Mexico, Canada, South Korea and Chile charge nothing on qualifying U.S. goods, and the EU, the largest market at $2.24B, has charged nothing on any Chapter 28 line since July 1, 2026.",
    "China's 10% extra duty, on top of its 2019 counter-tariffs, came as U.S. exports there fell 35.1% to $860M in 2025; rare-earth compounds have a 0% provisional rate for 2026 but still pay the 10%. Watch December 31, 2026 (China's exclusions end) and January 10, 2027 (its 24-point suspension ends).",
    "India's trade-remedy authority recommended soda ash import quotas on November 4, 2026, with 159,388 tonnes a year for U.S. supply, against 385,453 tonnes shipped in January–September 2025 alone; they apply only if the Government notifies them."
  ],
